# Lessons

Lessons learned, appended by `/post-op`. Commands read the section for the area they are about to work in.

Format:

- One `##` section per area (for example `## API`, `## Schema`, `## UI`, `## Tests`). Add a section when an area
  has its first lesson.
- One bullet per lesson: the rule, then a one-line why, then the ticket key in brackets.
- Write the rule so it applies next time, not the story of what happened.
- Before adding a lesson, search for one that already says it, and sharpen that one instead.
- If a lesson becomes a rule in `CLAUDE.md` or `.claude/rules/`, replace the bullet with a pointer to the rule.

